# Phase 59 Plan: Edit Setlist Items Texts

## Overview
Phase 59 introduces the ability to edit text and properties of setlist items directly from the setlist pane via a right-click context menu. The edits are saved exclusively within the setlist and do not alter the underlying Songs database or Bible database. Edited texts and references are applied across slides, preview pane, and live projections (overriding global chapter presentation options when edited).

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Design Points for Review:**
> 1. **Right-Click Context Menu**: Right-clicking any setlist item displays a sleek context menu with exactly one option: **'Edit'**.
> 2. **Edit Dialogs by Item Type**:
>    - **Image Slide**: Reuses existing `ImageSlideDialog` in edit mode.
>    - **Window Slide**: Reuses existing `WindowSlideDialog` in edit mode.
>    - **Song**: Opens `EditSongDialog` containing **Title** (single-line) and **Lyrics** (multi-line) textboxes with Cancel and Save buttons.
>    - **Scripture**: Opens `EditScriptureDialog` containing **Reference** (single-line) and **Verse** (multi-line) textboxes with Cancel and Save buttons.
>    - **Dual Scripture**: Opens `EditDualScriptureDialog` containing **Reference** (single-line, pre-filled with the current chapter presentation options Actual/Alias/None applied), **Primary Verse** (multi-line), and **Secondary Verse** (multi-line) textboxes with Cancel and Save buttons.
> 3. **Non-destructive Setlist Overrides**:
>    - Changes are persisted within the setlist only (using `SavedSetlist` / `itemOrder` serialization).
>    - The original database records for Songs and Bible chapters/verses remain completely untouched.
> 4. **Live Projection & Preview Override**:
>    - Edited scripture items have an `isEdited` flag that overrides global chapter presentation settings (`Actual`, `Alias`, `None`) on slides, preview pane, and live monitors (Monitor 1 and Monitor 2), displaying the user's custom reference directly.

